  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a downtrend or consolidation near support (e.g., 83-89 range), the model systematically overestimates by 5-10% because it ignores immediate mean reversion to historical averages.",
    "The model exhibits severe lag in reacting to sudden price spikes; true outcomes often surge 10-15% above forecasts within 7 days of a volatility event, regardless of prior sentiment neutrality.",
    "Sentiment history (values > 0.20) correlates with higher forecast accuracy only when the model correctly identifies a trend continuation; otherwise, high sentiment combined with flat recent prices leads to significant upward bias.",
    "The model fails to account for 'mean reversion' volatility, assuming linear growth from current levels while true outcomes frequently oscillate within a 15% band before breaking out.",
    "Forecasts are overly smooth and lack the necessary variance to capture sudden EU ETS supply shocks or demand surges that occur independently of sentiment history."
  ]
}
